From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WavJaby <WavJaby@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 09:25:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] libgui_aidl_types_rs: BitTube, LayerMetadata, VsyncEventData,
 ScreenCaptureResults

The crate's stand-ins for libgui's unstructured parcelables panic
(todo!()) as soon as one is read or written, so a Rust service of
android.gui.ISurfaceComposerClient / IDisplayEventConnection dies on
createSurface, stealReceiveChannel and getLatestVsyncEventData. Give
the four that the software path crosses their wire form:
LayerMetadata is read (count, then key and byte vector), BitTube is
written (the receive end, then the send end, each a bare fd object:
BitTube::writeToParcel), VsyncEventData (the Rust type that the AIDL
type ParcelableVsyncEventData names) is written as the words the caller
built, and ScreenCaptureResults is read and written: buffers and the
gain map as Parcel::write(Flattenable) framing, the fence as a Fence
or a status, the rest in libgui's wire order. The other stand-ins stay.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Patch-Reason: the stand-ins are AOSP's own Rust half of the interface and ship unimplemented; the launcher, loader and environment cannot supply a type that the generated AIDL code names by crate path (rust_type in the .aidl). A C++ adapter would need a cxx bridge inside this crate, so the codec is checked against libgui's own writer by the golden in atl-parcel-truth.
